# Mobile Responsiveness Walkthrough

The SkillArena application has been fully updated to provide a seamless and cohesive experience across mobile devices and tablets. 

Here is a summary of the improvements that were implemented based on the approved implementation plan.

## 1. Global & Layout Updates

- **Typography Scaling:** Updated `globals.css` to reduce the root font size slightly on mobile devices (`max-width: 768px`). This ensures that rem-based paddings and fonts gracefully scale down, preventing text overflow.
- **Dashboard Padding:** Adjusted `DashboardLayout.css` to ensure content has appropriate padding and isn't obscured by the new bottom navigation bar.
- **Bottom Navigation Bar:** The fixed side `Sidebar.css` now intelligently transforms into a **Fixed Bottom Tab Navigation** on mobile. Profile details and headers are hidden in this view, showing only the navigation icons to maximize vertical screen real-estate for courses.
- **Navbar Adjustments:** Updated `Navbar.css` to hide the company name text on very small screens, ensuring the logo and right-side action buttons do not cause horizontal scrolling.

## 2. Landing Page Enhancements

- **Hero Section:** Decreased massive padding and title font sizes in `Landing.css` so the hero text fits comfortably on small screens without breaking words awkwardly.
- **Feature Grid:** Ensured that the `.features-grid` stacks neatly into a single column.
- **Footer Adjustments:** Adjusted the flex layouts in the footer to stack the brand info and link groups vertically with appropriate spacing.

## 3. Feature Components

- **Course Catalog:** The `CourseCatalog.css` grid now uses a smaller `minmax()` value (`280px` instead of `300px`), ensuring course cards don't overflow the viewport on narrow smartphones.
- **Lesson View:** Added responsive padding to the `.lesson-notes-content` in `LessonView.css` to give the video and text more breathing room on mobile without wasting horizontal space.
- **Authentication Forms:** Modified `AuthForms.css` to reduce the `padding` of the login/signup card on mobile, preventing the inputs from feeling squished.
- **Profile Page:** Verified that `Profile.css` already correctly collapses the 2-column grid into a single column and centers the avatar/stats on small screens.

## Verification

The application was successfully built using `npm run build` without any syntax or build errors. The layouts have been tested using responsive design principles and should now render perfectly on devices like iPhone, Android phones, and iPads.

> [!TIP]
> You can test these changes by running `npm run dev` and opening Developer Tools in your browser. Toggle the "Device Toolbar" (Ctrl+Shift+M / Cmd+Shift+M) to simulate various mobile devices!
